    {
      "data": {
        "text": "All files have been implemented successfully. Here are the functionalities for each file:\n\n1. `summarize_text.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to summarize long text.\n2. `extract_json.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to extract structured JSON from text.\n3. `answer_with_context.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to answer a question using provided context.\n4. `stream_completion.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to stream partial output tokens from a hosted LLM.\n5. `model_client.py`: This file provides a utility function to get a client for the Google Cloud Language API.\n6. `model_models.py`: This file provides a utility function to create a request for the Google Cloud Language API.\n7. `prompt_safety.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to check prompts and generated text for unsafe content.\n8. `result_translate.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to translate generated model output.\n9. `output_embedding.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to embed model outputs for clustering or retrieval.\n10. `spoken_brief.py`: This file uses the Google Cloud Language API to generate a spoken brief from the model output.\n\nPlease note that you need to set the `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` environment variable to the path of your Google Cloud service account key file to authenticate with the Google Cloud Language API.",
